# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/

# Publish output
publish/
*.nupkg

# E2E evidence — regenerated by every `e2e` run
# Anchored: a bare "evidence/" would match a folder of that name at ANY
# depth — same trap as /sounds/ below.
/evidence/

# The full-size workbench (demo-full.bat regenerates it from scratch)
demo-full/

# Scratch audio: source material for the synthesized alert sounds. The ones
# the app actually ships live in src/OrdoSort.Wpf/Assets/sounds/.
# Anchored: a bare "sounds/" would match a folder of that name at ANY depth —
# including the shipped assets folder named in the line above.
/sounds/

# App runtime files
history.sqlite
history.sqlite-journal
history.sqlite-wal
history.sqlite-shm
crash.log
.env

# Claude Code session/agent state — never shipped, never reviewed
.claude/

# Real production/TAT exports used to design the report windows against live
# data. These contain REAL PATIENT NAMES and staff account names. They now live
# OUTSIDE this repo, at S:\OrdoSort-samples — an ignore rule only stops a
# commit, it does nothing about a tool that copies, greps, or uploads the
# working tree, so the data itself is kept out of the tree entirely. This rule
# stays as a safety net for the day someone drops a sample folder back in here.
.realSamples/

# The same thing, in the place it actually landed. On 2026-08-14 a folder of
# live exports — production dashboard.xlsx, TAT.xlsx, scan/mailroom/email
# report folders, ~15MB — was assembled under docs/ while putting a report
# fix together, and NONE of it matched any rule here: git check-ignore
# returned nothing for it. Nothing was committed, but only because the
# working tree happened to be inspected before the next `git add -A`.
#
# Same caveat as above, and it matters: an ignore rule only stops a commit.
# It does nothing about a tool that copies, greps, or uploads the working
# tree, and this repo has already had real patient data public for ~15 hours
# once. The data belongs outside the tree; this is the safety net, not the
# policy.
#
# That drop also produced loose archives at docs/*.zip (PAPER, c, i, sl).
# Not ignored here, deliberately — narrow rule, asked for narrowly. Widen it
# if that shape recurs.
docs/sample/

# Agent/skill tooling state dropped into the repo by installers and the
# brainstorming visual companion — local scratch, never reviewed.
.agents/
.superpowers/
skills-lock.json
evidence/

# Playwright MCP artifacts (screenshots/traces from ad-hoc browser testing)
.playwright-mcp/

# Stray screenshots dropped at the repo root by ad-hoc tooling. Real app/site
# image assets live in src/OrdoSort.Wpf/Assets/ and ordosort.com/assets/ (and
# docs/), never at the repo root — this is anchored so those are unaffected.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# Claude skills lockfile — personal tooling, not part of the app
skills-lock.json
